# L §4.5 (round 12): "A version or row known after on, or whose known window ends after it, is refused (LOAD-KNOWN):
# the reality can't know its own future, and on is its today"; L §8.3 LOAD-KNOWN `version <v> is known after the
# model's on date`. A version known in window(2026-01-01, 2026-12-31) in a model on 2026-10-18. (Was
# REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §4.5, writer 5's T-29.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input x: int

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known window(2026-01-01, 2026-12-31)
  x = 1

ask q: x
=== expect
refused: LOAD-KNOWN version v is known after the model's on date (m.tally:10)
